---
/**
 * Three requests of one turn: each the prefix and the journal read back whole (`flatMemory`), so each request is the
 * one before it with the last step's answer and results added at the end, and a provider's cache can serve all of the
 * earlier bytes.
 */
import Figure from "./Figure.astro"

const steps = [
  { label: "step 1", parts: [] as ReadonlyArray<string> },
  { label: "step 2", parts: ["answer 1", "results 1"] },
  { label: "step 3", parts: ["answer 1", "results 1", "answer 2", "results 2"] },
]
const X0 = 90
const PREFIX = 190
const TAIL = 70
const PART = 86
const y = (i: number) => 26 + i * 56
---

<Figure label="Why a turn's history is append-only" minWidth={720}>
  <svg class="rv-svg" viewBox="0 0 860 236" role="img" aria-labelledby="cd-t">
    <title id="cd-t">Each step's request is the previous request with the newest answer and tool results appended, so everything before them can come from the cache</title>
    {
      steps.map((s, i) => {
        const fresh = i === 0 ? 0 : 2
        return (
          <g>
            <text x="8" y={y(i) + 25} class="t-mono t-sm">{s.label}</text>
            <rect class="fill-accent" x={X0} y={y(i)} width={PREFIX} height="38" rx="5"></rect>
            <text x={X0 + PREFIX / 2} y={y(i) + 24} text-anchor="middle" class="t-xs">prefix (never stored)</text>
            <rect class={i === 0 ? "fill-new" : "fill-accent"} x={X0 + PREFIX + 4} y={y(i)} width={TAIL} height="38" rx="5"></rect>
            <text x={X0 + PREFIX + 4 + TAIL / 2} y={y(i) + 24} text-anchor="middle" class="t-xs">tail</text>
            {s.parts.map((p, j) => (
              <g>
                <rect class={j >= s.parts.length - fresh ? "fill-new" : "fill-accent"} x={X0 + PREFIX + TAIL + 8 + j * (PART + 4)} y={y(i)} width={PART} height="38" rx="5"></rect>
                <text x={X0 + PREFIX + TAIL + 8 + j * (PART + 4) + PART / 2} y={y(i) + 24} text-anchor="middle" class="t-xs">{p}</text>
              </g>
            ))}
          </g>
        )
      })
    }
    <rect class="fill-accent" x={X0} y="204" width="12" height="12" rx="2"></rect>
    <text x={X0 + 18} y="214" class="t-xs t-dim">the bytes of the request before: a provider's prompt cache may serve them</text>
    <rect class="fill-new" x={X0 + 470} y="204" width="12" height="12" rx="2"></rect>
    <text x={X0 + 488} y="214" class="t-xs t-dim">new at this step</text>
  </svg>
  <Fragment slot="caption">
    <strong>Nothing earlier is ever rewritten.</strong> The memory (<code>flatMemory</code> by default) reads the
    journal back whole, and the journal only grows at its end, so each request begins with every byte of the one
    before. A memory that dropped or summarised an earlier step would change the start of the request, and the cache
    would miss from that point on. At step 1 only the prefix can come from the cache, and only when an earlier turn
    or check of the same pull request sent it. Even the closing call keeps the same tools offered and the model's tool choice
    left as it was, since a narrower tool list changes the request ahead of the messages.
  </Fragment>
</Figure>
